#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
codex-usage: per-session Codex token/credit usage from local rollout JSONL files.

Reads:
  $CODEX_HOME/sessions/**/rollout-*.jsonl
  $CODEX_HOME/archived_sessions/**/rollout-*.jsonl
  $CODEX_HOME/state_5.sqlite   (optional, for thread titles)

No third-party Python packages required.

Examples:
  codex-usage today
  codex-usage yesterday
  codex-usage 6h
  codex-usage 12h
  codex-usage 24h
  codex-usage 48h
  codex-usage week
  codex-usage 7d
  codex-usage 2026-08-12
  codex-usage 2026-08-01..2026-08-12
  codex-usage today --show-subagents
  codex-usage today --fast
  codex-usage today --json
  codex-usage 24h --details --perf
  codex-usage 24h --wide
  codex-usage 24h --details --all-agents
  codex-usage --cache-info

Notes:
- `input_tokens` in Codex usage includes cached input tokens. Credit estimation
  charges only (input - cached) at the normal input rate, and cached input at
  the cached-input rate.
- reasoning_output_tokens is a subset/detail of output_tokens and is NOT added
  again when estimating credits.
- Fast/priority service tier is not reliably persisted in token_count JSONL
  events. `--fast` means "assume all eligible OpenAI-model usage in this
  report was Fast".
- Session JSONL is local telemetry, not the authoritative server-side meter.
- v1.4 adds native Windows support: Windows cache locations, Windows-safe
  SQLite read-only URIs, automatic VT/ANSI terminal enablement, PowerShell/CMD
  launchers, and Windows CI coverage. macOS and Linux behavior is preserved.
"""

